  "n": 33,
  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v1 drafted",
  "phase": "DISCOVER",
  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 104,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets more than doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to 1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026). The dominant mechanism is a billing import/validation defect: a majority of disputed bills (1785 of 3025) are based on accepted ACTUAL meter reads rather than estimate-substitution, showing wrong bills are produced during billing import/validation processing itself (not by read acquisition alone), consistent with a change to validation rules around August. Separately, manual-read route completion fell to 88% against a 95% target, contributing estimate-substitution errors to the remaining ESTIMATED-read disputes. The surge is not explained by response-handling capacity (CS already within SLA) nor by a tariff change (none logged) nor by AMI pipeline failure (ruled out by actual-read dominance)."
 },
